    "body": "You might be thinking of the git repo tests, which fail for me locally too:\r\nhttps://github.com/starship/starship/blob/d36d232cc6a2987263dacbbe293af624d647cdb3/tests/directory.rs#L100-L134\r\n\r\nI'm still not 100% sure why they fail locally. I have yet to use a debugger to step through those tests to see why they fail, but they seem to pass as expected in CI. 🤔 \r\n\r\nThese new `ignore` attributes were added because the directory is expected to exist for real, now that we read the directory on `Context` creation.\r\nhttps://github.com/starship/starship/blob/d36d232cc6a2987263dacbbe293af624d647cdb3/src/context.rs#L26-L35\r\n\r\nThis wouldn't be a problem if we could mock the output of `fs::read_dir`, but I don't think Rust provides us with a very easy way to do that. 😅 \r\n\r\nI'm going to create an issue where we can further discuss test strategy.",
